(e774fcbf745d8a55afb999ad9ab4e87cbce2a850src/LinuxHotas/2#cheezecake-dev/CheezecakeLinuxHotas
$44E8E046-B17D-41AB-80DB-D9686350F95ACheezecake's Linux HOTAS*[Early release: fly with joysticks, a separate stick and throttle included, on native Linux.2
Cheezecake: EARLY RELEASE, not yet tried with a physical HOTAS. Fly with joysticks on native Linux (Interim, no Proton), flat or in VR with Cheezecake's SE VR.

- Every joystick, throttle and pedal set at once, read straight from the kernel; devices can come and go while the game runs
- Axes add to the keyboard, mouse and VR hands: move, pitch, yaw, roll and the camera
- Buttons and hats: fire, target lock, lights, dampeners, handbrake, power, parking, wheel jump, brakes, toolbar
- Wheels: steering, drive force by throttle (single player or a lobby you host), and a brake lever
- Programmable blocks named [AnalogThrottle] get wolfe's AnalogThrottle format, so his scripts work unchanged

Set up binds under Plugin settings. On Windows, use ananace's Analog Grid Control instead.

Bug reports: https://github.com/cheezecake-dev/CheezecakeLinuxHotasBCoreCLRRLinux
