(cbfbad002e661815b2865ec12ece4956d0cfb5b1ClientPluginShared2blazeblue32/WaterShading
$b90210a0-0138-415c-8af6-5ce1cede7350Water Shading*ZMakes the Water Mod's sea take sun shadows and the planet's atmospheric haze into account.2BlazeBlue32:Companion to the Water Mod (Steam Workshop 2200451495). The mod draws the sea as particles, which the game neither shadows nor covers with the planet's atmosphere: mountain and ship shadows never fall on the water, and the sea looks pasted over the haze. This plugin tags the sea's particles by material, makes the particle shader read the sun shadow map for each of their pixels, and adds the planet's atmospheric haze to them as the game does for terrain. The first ten to fifteen seconds in a world may stutter for the first launch or two while the graphics layer builds the changed shaders; it settles on later launches.
Ã∫G
(a50c8ada5151ad85aef89be6e844bb8899dc634f2dawidmachon/se-welder-paint
dawidmachon/se-welder-paintWelder Paint*FPaint blocks by aiming a welder at them instead of using a ghost block2dawidmachon:ˇRepaint blocks by aiming your welder at them and pressing the left mouse button - no need to hold a block in hand and touch its sides with the ghost, which is tedious for small or decorative blocks.

Pick a color or skin in the normal color picker (P) as usual, toggle paint mode with a configurable keybind (default O), aim, click. Hold the left mouse button to paint continuously.

Targeting mirrors the welder's own highlight, so visually small blocks that own a whole cube cell (corner floor lamps, wall pictures) can be painted directly or aimed past to paint the floor/wall behind them.

Uses the exact same server-validated paint request as vanilla block painting, so multiplayer ownership rules apply unchanged. Optional debug network logging for diagnostics.
